From: Droidspaces container adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt MangoHud metrics to a Droidspaces container
A Droidspaces container runs on real Qualcomm hardware but does not mount
the whole sysfs tree, so several of the metrics the armada patch set reads
are simply absent:
  * /sys/class/hwmon does not exist, so the msm GPU hwmon node (power,
    fan, vrm temp) is unreachable and the CPU sensor list is empty;
  * the kernel exposes the older kgsl-3d0 layout, where the GPU clock is
    `clock_mhz` (MHz) instead of devfreq `cur_freq` (Hz).
The armada set reads only `cur_freq`, so inside a container the GPU clock,
load and temperature all read 0 and the overlay is useless.
Changes:
  * init_kgsl(): probe clock_mhz, cur_freq, gpu_busy_percentage and temp,
    opening whichever exist instead of assuming one layout.
  * get_kgsl_clock(): scale per unit (MHz vs Hz) via a recorded flag.
  * init_thermal_zone_fallback()/get_thermal_zone_temp(): when neither
    KGSL nor hwmon yields a GPU temperature, read the gpuss-N thermal
    zone the kernel still publishes.
  * file_utils ls(): a missing directory is ENOENT, not an error; log at
    debug so the overlay does not spam the journal every scan.
  * CPU power via the kernel EAS energy model: this target exposes neither
    hwmon nor a populated powercap, so cpu_power always read 0. The kernel
    does publish a vendor-calibrated power table per CPU performance
    domain in /sys/kernel/debug/energy_model, plus per-OPP residency in
    cpufreq/stats/time_in_state. get_cpu_power_energy_model() combines
    the two into a residency-weighted average, which is the same model the
    Android power HAL uses. Registered as CPU_POWER_ENERGY_MODEL and tried
    after hwmon, APU and powercap all fail, so bare-metal behaviour is
    unchanged.
Note: the energy model lives in debugfs, whose mountpoint is mode 0700.
Reading it therefore needs either root or `chmod 755 /sys/kernel/debug`.
Without that access the source simply fails to initialise and cpu_power
stays hidden, exactly as before.

